FINDINGS:
1. [MAJOR] src/repl/completer.rs:294 — `quote_if_spaced(&entry_name)` is concatenated with the trailing `/` *outside* the quotes, so a directory whose name contains a space is offered as `"my dir"/` — a form that is broken twice over: (a) the next TAB cannot walk into it, because `split_fragment` (completer.rs:247) returns `"my dir/"` as the directory and `dir.join(directory)` (completer.rs:280) then reads a path whose name literally begins and ends with `"`, so `read_dir` fails and TAB offers nothing; (b) the completed line cannot be loaded at all, because `ReplCommand::unquote_path` (src/repl/commands.rs:558) only strips a *matching* pair and `"my dir"/` ends with `/`, so the quote survives into `fs::read_to_string`. Verified on this tree: `complete_path_in(dir, "my")` → `["\"my dir\"/", "\"my file.rb\""]`, `complete_path_in(dir, "\"my dir/")` → `[]`, and `printf ':load "/tmp/…/my dir"/sub/a.rb\n' | ./target/debug/rb` answers `Could not load file: No such file or directory (os error 2)` while the hand-typed `"/tmp/…/my dir/sub/a.rb"` works. This directly contradicts the module's own promise at completer.rs:265-267 ("a trailing separator … lets the next TAB walk in"). `edge_a_filename_with_a_space_in_it_is_offered_quoted` (completer.rs:838) pins only the offer and passes on the broken feature, and nothing tests accept-or-descend. Fix: build the candidate from an unquoted name and quote only the final joined path (or strip a matched pair when re-reading the fragment in `split_fragment`), plus a test that accepts `"my dir/"` and completes a file inside it.
2. [MAJOR] src/repl/transcript.rs:222 — `push_line` uses `blocks[index].is_empty()` as its "no line pushed yet" sentinel, so a block whose *first* line is empty loses that line: the first `push_line` writes `""` (still empty), the second sees `is_empty()` and writes without the separator. Verified: `Transcript::markdown()` of an exchange whose input is `"\nsay \"one\"\nsay \"two\""` reads back as `["say \"one\"\nsay \"two\""]`. This is reachable from Redblue source — `:load file.rb` where the file begins with a blank line (extremely common) — and the document itself is correct, so it is only the reader half that is wrong, which is precisely the invariant the phase exists to establish (transcript.rs:14-16, and `a_session_read_back_from_its_own_markdown_is_the_session` at transcript.rs:394 which passes only because its fixtures have no leading blank). A 2×(all-cases) sweep over tick-run/suffix combinations found this is the *only* input-side round-trip mismatch left after the fence fix, so it is the residual hole, not a duplicate of the one fixed. Fix: track whether a line has been pushed (e.g. `Option<String>` per block, or a parallel line count) instead of testing emptiness; add the missing test `:load` of a file starting with a blank line round-tripping.
3. [MINOR] src/repl/completer.rs:840 — `path_argument(":loa\u{1F600}", 4)` is asserted with the message "and a cursor inside a character is not one either", but `pos == 4` is a *valid* char boundary: `":loa😀".get(..4) == Some(":loa")`. The guard under test (`line.get(..pos)?` at completer.rs:232, added to stop a panic) is never exercised; the non-boundary offsets are 5, 6 and 7. The assertion passes for the wrong reason — it returns `None` because `head.find(char::is_whitespace)` found nothing. Fix: assert `path_argument(":loa\u{1F600}", 5)` (and 6/7) so the non-boundary slice is the thing being pinned.
4. [MINOR] phases/phase-060/REPORT.md:118 — the report states "Over the whole phase (`git diff 222aa83..HEAD` plus the working tree) it is **+3195 −24** across 11 files". `git diff --shortstat 222aa83..HEAD` in this tree is `11 files changed, 3460 insertions(+), 24 deletions(-)`; +3195 −24 is `222aa83..28398c0`, i.e. the range before this run's own commit. The number attributed to a named command is wrong by 265 lines. Harmless to behaviour, but a report whose stated diffstat does not match the command it names is the same class of unverifiable claim the reviewer contract exists to catch. Fix: quote `28398c0..HEAD` (491/226) and `222aa83..HEAD` (3460/24) as two separate numbers.
5. [STYLE] tests/repl_test.rs:1345 — `plain()` re-implements escape stripping with a different rule from the one this phase added to `src/repl/style.rs` for exactly this purpose: `strip_escapes` (style.rs:251) ends a CSI at any final byte in `@`…`~`, while `plain` scans forward until it sees an `m` and discards everything up to it. On a session that emitted `\u{1b}[2J`, `plain` swallows the following real output. The whole point of promoting `strip_escapes` to a shared helper is that an export, a test and a `--color=never` pipe all want the same answer; a second, weaker copy in the test file is the three-places-to-get-it-wrong problem the helper's own doc comment (style.rs:242-245) was written to prevent. Fix: call `redblue::repl::style::strip_escapes` from `plain` and delete the copy.

